# Workers static assets headers. Format: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/
#
# What stays open: script-src keeps 'unsafe-inline', so an injected <script>
# element would still run (and could read the commenter token comments.ts keeps
# in localStorage). The pages ship inline <script> blocks, and Cloudflare
# injects its own inline bot-detection script whose body changes on every
# request, so no hash can cover it, and a static _headers file cannot carry a
# nonce. The CSP is defence in depth behind the escaping in the markdown
# renderer and the comment thread. style-src keeps 'unsafe-inline' too, for the
# inline style attributes.
#
# What it closes: inline event handler attributes (script-src-attr 'none';
# handlers are bound from scripts, and src/csp.test.ts plus the CI smoke check
# keep it that way), scripts and stylesheets from anything but the pinned CDN
# paths, and the frame-ancestors / base-uri / object-src pivots. jsDelivr and
# cdnjs host every npm package, so script-src names the exact GSAP 3.13.0,
# Lenis 1.3.25, Twemoji 14.0.2 and Prism 1.29.0 paths, and style-src only
# Prism's themes/ directory, instead of the whole hosts. A version bump in the
# markup needs its path updated here; src/csp.test.ts fails until it is.
#
# The connect allowlist is kept tight too: the API origin and the two telemetry
# integrations below. Stale entries — cdn.tailwindcss.com (now build-time
# PostCSS), the Google ad domains (no ads), the origin-locked *.fly.dev, the
# unused ad frame-src, and the three public feeds the retired ANNEX D
# live-telemetry strip polled (ISS position, USGS quakes, Frankfurter FX) —
# were removed: they served no live resource and only widened the attack
# surface.
#
# frame-src (YouTube): the /videos Shorts rail injects a youtube-nocookie
# embed when a card is played — the site's only iframe. Without this entry
# frames fall back to default-src 'self' and Chrome blocks the player outright
# ("This content is blocked"), which is exactly what happened when the rail
# shipped. www.youtube.com is listed alongside because some Shorts playback
# flows hand off to that origin. Note this cannot be caught by `npm run dev`:
# public/_headers is applied by Workers static assets, so no CSP exists locally.
#
# Sentry (connect-src): sentry.client.config.js initialises with
# PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN in prod, so error envelopes POST to the ingest endpoint.
# Without this entry every send is refused and client-side monitoring silently
# reports nothing. Pinned to the project's exact ingest origin rather than a
# *.ingest.us.sentry.io wildcard, so a compromised script cannot exfiltrate to
# an unrelated Sentry tenant.
#
# Cloudflare Web Analytics (script-src + connect-src): the beacon is injected
# at the edge by Web Analytics "automatic setup" — there is no reference to it
# anywhere in this repo, so grep will not explain these two entries. It needs
# BOTH: the script loads from static.cloudflareinsights.com, then POSTs its
# measurements to a DIFFERENT host, cloudflareinsights.com/cdn-cgi/rum. The
# privacy policy discloses this analytics; if the edge setting is ever turned
# off, drop these entries and that disclosure together.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.13.0/dist/ https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/lenis@1.3.25/dist/lenis.min.js https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/twemoji@14.0.2/dist/twemoji.min.js https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/prism/1.29.0/ https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; script-src-attr 'none'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/prism/1.29.0/themes/ https://fonts.googleapis.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com data:; connect-src 'self' https://api.luci-studio.com https://o4509530171113472.ingest.us.sentry.io https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://www.youtube.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; form-action 'self'
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
